WEBVTT

00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:26.629
BOIMLER:
Ensign Boimler, personal log,

00:01:26.672 --> 00:01:29.066
stardate 57601.3.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.938
TheCerritos is in orbit
around Mixtus III to assist

00:01:31.982 --> 00:01:34.550
in a controlled demolition
of an unstable moon.

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:36.073
We're providing support
to theVancouver,

00:01:36.117 --> 00:01:38.293
aParliament-class ship
which focuses

00:01:38.336 --> 00:01:41.339
on complex, large-scale
engineering projects.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.603
Welcome, Captain. Take it in.

00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:47.606
One day you could be in command
of a vessel like the Vancouver.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:51.567
Thank you, Captain. This is
truly a humbling experience.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.046
You're welcome.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.875
Unfortunately, we might have
to cancel the demolition.

00:01:55.919 --> 00:01:57.790
-What? Why?
-Is the moon too dense?

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.315
No, it's more
of a diplomatic issue.

00:02:00.358 --> 00:02:03.013
Diplomatic? Isn't the moon goingto plummet into the planet

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:06.321
-and ignite the atmosphere?
-And, you know, kill everyone?

00:02:06.364 --> 00:02:08.366
I've told them that many times,
but they simply don't care.

00:02:10.412 --> 00:02:12.022
-You don't know
what you're talking...
-Of all the moons we pray to,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.893
that's one
of the most important!

00:02:13.937 --> 00:02:15.808
It controls the tides
for our summer crop.

00:02:15.852 --> 00:02:18.681
My family has lived
on that moon for generations.

00:02:18.724 --> 00:02:20.030
Moons can't plummet.
That's something the government

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.511
-made up to control us.

00:02:22.554 --> 00:02:24.643
Ooh, boy.

00:02:24.687 --> 00:02:27.516
BOIMLER: So the moon's decaying
orbit could cause catastrophic

00:02:27.559 --> 00:02:28.995
blah, blah, blah,
blah, blah-- okay, okay.

00:02:29.039 --> 00:02:31.868
The real news is I get to
have lunch with the coolest,

00:02:31.911 --> 00:02:35.350
smartest officer in Starfleet,
Barbara Brinson,

00:02:35.393 --> 00:02:39.354
who also happens
to be my girlfriend.

00:02:39.397 --> 00:02:40.920
That's right. Ugh!

00:02:40.964 --> 00:02:42.792
We met a month ago
and it's just been magical.

00:02:42.835 --> 00:02:44.837
Ooh, boy, here we go.

00:02:44.881 --> 00:02:47.057
Log number one million
about Girlfriend Barb.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.885
You know, I am sorry,
but I'm starting to think

00:02:48.928 --> 00:02:50.539
that Barb might
not actually exist.

00:02:50.582 --> 00:02:52.410
Oh, she's real.

00:02:52.454 --> 00:02:55.152
She's as real as a hopped-up
Q on Captain Picard Day.

00:02:55.196 --> 00:02:56.849
Let me guess, when we meet her,

00:02:56.893 --> 00:02:59.112
it'll weirdly have to be
on the holodeck.

00:02:59.156 --> 00:03:01.071
Hey. I don't do that anymore.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.378
-Okay?
-Sure you don't, man.
But just so you know,

00:03:03.421 --> 00:03:05.554
-I am still gonna try
waving my hand through her.
-Please don't.

00:03:05.597 --> 00:03:07.077
-I'm gonna.
-You're gonna hit skin.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.122
Well, if I do,it's the cost of doing business.

00:03:10.472 --> 00:03:12.648
Ooh. You smell that, Tendi?

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:15.651
Each ship on the fleet
has its own scent.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:17.174
I think the Cerritossmells like

00:03:17.218 --> 00:03:18.915
toasting marshmallows
on a cool night.

00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:20.612
Is that a plasma fire?

00:03:20.656 --> 00:03:22.092
Huh? Oh-- uh, uh...

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.963
The D53 probably sparked again.

00:03:24.007 --> 00:03:25.661
They're so buggy.

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:27.184
Yeah, the whole ship's
kind of falling apart.

00:03:27.228 --> 00:03:29.795
Yep, this old girl's
seen a lot of light-years.

00:03:29.839 --> 00:03:31.144
You know, Kula told me
the Vancouver

00:03:31.188 --> 00:03:32.624
has fluidic processors

00:03:32.668 --> 00:03:34.060
that self-replicate
their own silicas.

00:03:34.104 --> 00:03:35.453
Nuh-uh!

00:03:35.497 --> 00:03:36.933
And he said they had
tritanium hull brackets.

00:03:36.976 --> 00:03:39.588
-And get this: T88s.
-That can't be right.

00:03:39.631 --> 00:03:41.067
-T88s aren't even out yet.
-I know.

00:03:41.111 --> 00:03:43.461
It's a starship, not heaven.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.464
I can't believe it.

00:03:46.508 --> 00:03:49.032
This is the greatest ship
I've ever seen.

00:03:49.075 --> 00:03:51.469
Are you kidding me?
This is amazing.

00:03:51.513 --> 00:03:54.820
Uh, guys? It's basically, like,
the same ship as the Cerritos.

00:03:54.864 --> 00:03:57.606
-Yeah, right.

00:03:57.649 --> 00:03:59.129
Ooh, let's go look
at their thermal mesh.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.522
I bet it's a double lattice!

00:04:00.565 --> 00:04:02.045
-Double lattice!

00:04:02.088 --> 00:04:04.787
Where's Barb?
She said she'd meet me here.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.658
Oh, this is too sad. Hey, look.

00:04:06.702 --> 00:04:08.791
I can set you up with somebody
great on the Cerritos.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.009
There's that
Phylosian in tactical.

00:04:10.053 --> 00:04:11.184
She seems like
a nice plant person.

00:04:11.228 --> 00:04:12.534
BARB:
 Brad!

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.148
Uh, wha-- Uh, c-computer,
end program.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.195
I missed you so much.

00:04:22.239 --> 00:04:23.545
-Ugh.

00:04:23.588 --> 00:04:25.155
-Mmm.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.549
-We kissed, did you see?
-Hi. Sorry.

00:04:27.592 --> 00:04:30.552
It's been a long month.
I'm Lieutenant Barbara Brinson.

00:04:30.595 --> 00:04:32.162
Um, yeah-- I'm, uh,
I'm Beckett Mariner,

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:34.643
-and this is Boimler.
-: Yeah, I know.

00:04:34.686 --> 00:04:36.209
Oh! I can't wait
to show you everything.

00:04:36.253 --> 00:04:37.602
Come on.

00:04:37.646 --> 00:04:39.648
She's a lieutenant?

00:04:39.691 --> 00:04:41.519
BARB:
You know, whatever,
it was no big deal.

00:04:41.563 --> 00:04:42.694
I managed to reverse
the polarity

00:04:42.738 --> 00:04:44.130
and reboot the time stream.

00:04:44.174 --> 00:04:47.133
Good thing, too,
'cause, oof, 1920s Chicago?

00:04:47.177 --> 00:04:49.135
-Nobody's washing their hands.

00:04:49.179 --> 00:04:51.181
Oh, I love that story, bun-bun.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.879
-Mwah, mwah.
-Wow, all that's so amazing.

00:04:53.923 --> 00:04:56.012
And now you date Brad.

00:04:56.055 --> 00:04:58.884
Ugh, I know. I swore
I'd never do long-distance.

00:04:58.928 --> 00:05:01.887
But then I met this goofball
on Vendu last month.

00:05:01.931 --> 00:05:05.717
He radiates a primal confidence.I'm sure you've felt it.

00:05:05.761 --> 00:05:07.676
No, I try not to feel
anything around Brad.

00:05:07.719 --> 00:05:09.504
-Barbasaurus Rex!
-Jet?

00:05:09.547 --> 00:05:11.114
Get up here.We're gonna be working together.

00:05:11.157 --> 00:05:13.290
-Ah! Whoa.
-Uh...

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:15.553
-Really?
-Okay, you can maybe
put her down now.

00:05:15.597 --> 00:05:17.294
-Like, anytime.
-Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:05:17.338 --> 00:05:19.165
Did you hear some purple people
are throwing a tantrum?

00:05:19.209 --> 00:05:20.819
Implosion's been postponed.

00:05:20.863 --> 00:05:23.518
We got to recalibrate the whole
goddamn containment field.

00:05:23.561 --> 00:05:25.041
Oh, Boim-Boim.

00:05:25.084 --> 00:05:27.043
Looks like I can't do lunch
on the Cerritos.

00:05:27.086 --> 00:05:28.958
Oh, no, it's fine.
It's not like I programmed

00:05:29.001 --> 00:05:30.612
a ten-course meal or anything.

00:05:30.655 --> 00:05:31.961
Hey. See you in Engineering.

00:05:32.004 --> 00:05:34.311
And I'll try not
to bring it downtown.

00:05:34.355 --> 00:05:35.878
-Shut up.

00:05:35.921 --> 00:05:37.706
-No, you shut up.
-Shut up.
-Huh?

00:05:37.749 --> 00:05:39.272
Ow. Ow, no, you shut up. Stop.

00:05:39.316 --> 00:05:40.970
Wait, how do you know Jet?

00:05:41.013 --> 00:05:43.189
He's, like, the second
coolest person on the Cerritos.

00:05:43.233 --> 00:05:45.061
Ugh, we dated, like,
a billion years ago.

00:05:45.104 --> 00:05:47.890
-What?
-But he's nothing compared
to my Bradward.

00:05:47.933 --> 00:05:51.067
: Oh!
Your real name is Bradward?

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:53.069
Yeah, I'm a Bradward. There's
Bradleys, there's Bradwards.

00:05:53.112 --> 00:05:56.246
It feels so good to be near you.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:59.118
-BOTH: Mwah!

00:05:59.162 --> 00:06:01.730
Well, I got to hand it to you.
You were right.

00:06:01.773 --> 00:06:03.253
Barb is great.

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.864
A little too great.

00:06:06.952 --> 00:06:08.824
Hey. Ron Docent.
Welcome aboard

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:09.912
the Vancouver.

00:06:09.955 --> 00:06:11.304
She's a beaut, isn't she?

00:06:11.348 --> 00:06:12.305
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:12.349 --> 00:06:13.829
So, the captain,
your captain,

00:06:13.872 --> 00:06:16.092
has ordered us to look
for alternatives to implosion.

00:06:16.135 --> 00:06:17.789
I'm gonna have you two
run diagnostics

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:19.138
on the simulation mainframe.

00:06:19.182 --> 00:06:21.314
You both comfortable using T88s?

00:06:21.358 --> 00:06:22.315
Yes, sir.
So comfortable.

00:06:22.359 --> 00:06:23.621
Supercomfortable.

00:06:23.665 --> 00:06:25.144
-Ha. I like that enthusiasm.

00:06:25.188 --> 00:06:26.798
Tell you what,
whoever finishes first

00:06:26.842 --> 00:06:29.105
gets their very own T88.

00:06:29.148 --> 00:06:30.628
Wait. You mean, like,
we get to keep them?

00:06:30.672 --> 00:06:31.977
Or-or is this, like,
a borrow thing?

00:06:32.021 --> 00:06:33.326
Like, we're gonna have
to give them back, right?

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.764
Nope. I mean keep,
like "you keep it."

00:06:35.807 --> 00:06:36.852
-Ah!
-Sorry, sir.

00:06:36.895 --> 00:06:38.636
Just checking
if this is a dream.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.072
I've got a bad feeling
about Barb.

00:06:40.116 --> 00:06:42.248
I know. I can't believe
she used to date Jet!

00:06:42.292 --> 00:06:44.816
That guy's like a Kirk sundae
with Trip Tucker sprinkles.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:46.209
I'm not messing around.

00:06:46.252 --> 00:06:47.906
Barb is way, way,
wayout of your league.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.386
Not out of Jet's league.
I...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.736
Uh, I-I got to get jacked.
Here we go.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.869
Brad, when
a Starfleet relationship

00:06:53.912 --> 00:06:55.348
-seems too good
to be true, then...

00:06:55.392 --> 00:06:56.959
red alert, man-- it probably is.

00:06:57.002 --> 00:06:58.395
You think she's cheating on me?!

00:06:58.439 --> 00:07:01.137
No! I think she's a secret alien
who's gonna eat you

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.400
or a Romulan spy
or a salt succubus

00:07:03.444 --> 00:07:04.706
or an android or a changeling

00:07:04.749 --> 00:07:06.403
or one of those sexy people
in rompers

00:07:06.447 --> 00:07:08.187
that murders you
just for going on the grass!

00:07:08.231 --> 00:07:09.711
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
I'm sorry, you're saying

00:07:09.754 --> 00:07:11.887
that because Barb is awesome
and hot and dating me

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.018
that she's an alien?

00:07:13.062 --> 00:07:14.106
That is messed up, Mariner!

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.325
That is not cool.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.413
This is real, Bradward.

00:07:16.457 --> 00:07:18.154
I have seen stuff, man.

00:07:18.197 --> 00:07:21.810
Like back when I was serving
on the Quito...

00:07:23.725 --> 00:07:25.248
You guys...

00:07:25.291 --> 00:07:27.424
Ooh, you hear what happened
on the Enterprise?

00:07:27.468 --> 00:07:29.339
Apparently,
Data's got an evil twin brother

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:30.906
who teamed up with the Borg.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:32.516
-Crazy, right?

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.301
What? Man, it's like a new thingevery week with those guys.

00:07:35.345 --> 00:07:37.652
Right. Like, leave some unknown
for the rest of us.

00:07:39.784 --> 00:07:41.960
Aw, you guys
are such a great couple.

00:07:42.004 --> 00:07:43.005
Oh, what can I say?

00:07:43.048 --> 00:07:44.441
I found the perfect guy.

00:07:44.485 --> 00:07:46.182
Look, I'm not perfect, okay?

00:07:46.225 --> 00:07:48.097
But I do have
the perfect friends.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.360
Uh, no, Niko,
you are the nicest, smartest,

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.144
handsomest guy on this ship.

00:07:52.188 --> 00:07:53.276
I mean, it's either that

00:07:53.319 --> 00:07:54.973
or you're
a Harvongian shape-changer.

00:07:56.235 --> 00:07:59.064
I mean, you're too handsome.

00:07:59.108 --> 00:08:00.718
-Niko?

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:05.462
-No!

00:08:05.506 --> 00:08:08.160
Shape-changer!

00:08:08.204 --> 00:08:09.161
Angie!

00:08:09.205 --> 00:08:10.859
No...!

00:08:10.902 --> 00:08:13.209
I'm not gonna sit around
and let a face get melted.

00:08:13.252 --> 00:08:14.340
Not again.

00:08:14.384 --> 00:08:15.472
You're not leaving my sight,
mister.

00:08:15.516 --> 00:08:16.995
Every minute
Barb spends with Jet

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:18.257
puts me closer to losing her.

00:08:18.301 --> 00:08:19.432
I got to do something.

00:08:19.476 --> 00:08:22.218
And so do I.

00:08:30.008 --> 00:08:32.228
Okay, listen up!
We will relocate

00:08:32.271 --> 00:08:34.665
three tons of moon dust
for people to worship.

00:08:34.709 --> 00:08:37.102
The farmers will have gravitysystems installed for the tides.

00:08:37.146 --> 00:08:39.148
And you three,
your ancestral homes

00:08:39.191 --> 00:08:41.237
will be relocated
to the sixth moon,

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.892
which will now technically
be the fifth anyway.

00:08:43.935 --> 00:08:45.676
Does that work for everyone?

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.896
-Yeah.
-It works for me.
-Okay.

00:08:49.419 --> 00:08:51.421
No, you don't understand.

00:08:51.464 --> 00:08:53.945
This moon blocks pollution
from Mixtus III

00:08:53.989 --> 00:08:55.773
from reaching my people
on Mixtus II.

00:08:55.817 --> 00:08:58.341
Without this moon, we'll perish.

00:08:58.384 --> 00:08:59.472
But if we don't destroy it,

00:08:59.516 --> 00:09:01.387
the folks on Mixtus III
will perish.

00:09:01.431 --> 00:09:04.042
I know.
It's an impossible problem.

00:09:04.086 --> 00:09:06.001
Well, we're Starfleet.

00:09:06.044 --> 00:09:08.090
Figuring out impossible problemsis what we do,

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:11.136
so let's just keep calm
and, uh, try

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.399
-to think of a solution.
-No! If you blow up that moon,

00:09:13.443 --> 00:09:15.401
you're murderers!You'll have blood on your hands!

00:09:15.445 --> 00:09:17.229
Shut up and let me think!

00:09:18.274 --> 00:09:20.058
All right, listen up, everybody.

00:09:20.102 --> 00:09:22.408
Each of our orbital platforms
will maintain

00:09:22.452 --> 00:09:24.715
-a tractor spread
to control lunar debris.
-Ha!

00:09:24.759 --> 00:09:27.065
"Da Brie"?
What is this, a cheese party?

00:09:27.109 --> 00:09:29.807
Hey, babe, it's me. Whoop.

00:09:29.851 --> 00:09:32.157
Okay, okay. Yep.

00:09:32.201 --> 00:09:34.464
-Okay.
-Hey, don't worry, buddy.
I got it.

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:36.205
All right.

00:09:36.248 --> 00:09:38.468
-Thank you, Jet.
-No worries.

00:09:38.511 --> 00:09:40.513
Uh, Brad, um,
what are you doing here?

00:09:40.557 --> 00:09:44.387
Oh, you know, just wanted to seemy girlfriend do her thang.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.171
Yeah, we're together.

00:09:46.215 --> 00:09:48.217
Uh, anyway,
getting back to the demo...

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.305
-Aah!

00:09:49.348 --> 00:09:50.915
Aah!

00:09:50.959 --> 00:09:52.438
Whoa, whoa, stop it! Stop it!

00:09:52.482 --> 00:09:53.962
Turn it off.
What are you doing?!

00:09:54.005 --> 00:09:55.441
Whoopsies! Sorry. New tricorder.

00:09:55.485 --> 00:09:57.095
Okay, she's not an android,
'cause that tone

00:09:57.139 --> 00:09:58.923
would have disrupted
her positronic brain.

00:09:58.967 --> 00:10:01.360
Whatever she is, she's organic.
Okay, I have to get a sample.

00:10:01.404 --> 00:10:02.971
-Okay, we're gonna...
You're gonna leave now.
-I got to...

00:10:03.014 --> 00:10:04.929
Sorry, guys.
Mariner was just leaving.

00:10:04.973 --> 00:10:07.149
Actually,
maybe you should go with her.

00:10:07.192 --> 00:10:08.454
We've just got a lot to cover.

00:10:08.498 --> 00:10:11.066
Oh. But I didn't get
to see you do your thang.

00:10:11.109 --> 00:10:12.894
So sweet of you to come by.

00:10:12.937 --> 00:10:14.460
I'll meet you later
in the mess, okay?

00:10:14.504 --> 00:10:15.984
Yeah, yeah, no,
the mission comes first.

00:10:16.027 --> 00:10:17.768
-Totally. I'll just, you know...-

00:10:17.812 --> 00:10:19.465
-JET: What I'm talking about.
-BARB: Oh.

00:10:19.509 --> 00:10:22.338
I hope
we never blow up that moon.

00:10:22.381 --> 00:10:24.340
These T88s are amazing.

00:10:24.383 --> 00:10:25.558
Yeah, they're, like, crazy fast.

00:10:25.602 --> 00:10:27.125
How many diagnostics
have you run?

00:10:27.169 --> 00:10:29.345
15. Oh, when I come back
with this baby,

00:10:29.388 --> 00:10:31.347
the guys in Engineering
are gonna flip.

00:10:34.916 --> 00:10:36.787
Yeah, right. It'sgonna be me who takes this back.

00:10:36.831 --> 00:10:38.397
I'm gonna blow their minds
in Medical.

00:10:40.443 --> 00:10:41.444
RUTHERFORD:
Nope.

00:10:41.487 --> 00:10:43.838
-16.
-22.

00:10:44.969 --> 00:10:46.405
17. 18.

00:10:46.449 --> 00:10:47.842
-19. 20. 21.
-N-N-No!

00:10:47.885 --> 00:10:48.973
-Hey, don't you use
your implant.
-22.

00:10:49.017 --> 00:10:50.192
-That's not fair!
-Ooh, 23!

00:10:50.235 --> 00:10:52.324
I got to figure this out.
I got to... Wait!

00:10:52.368 --> 00:10:54.936
Okay, okay, okay.
